{"step_index":371,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T11:41:47Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-25T17:11:47+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-25T17:11:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/app.js`\nTotal Lines: 1230\nTotal Bytes: 49748\nShowing lines 810 to 880\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n810:     });\n811:   }\n812: \n813:   /* =========================================================\n814:      AREA 3: SCOPE ISOLATION & STACK/HEAP MEMORY MODEL\n815:      ========================================================= */\n816:   renderArea3MemoryAndScopes(step) {\n817:     this.scopeFramesContainer.innerHTML = \"\";\n818:     this.heapObjectsContainer.innerHTML = \"\";\n819:     this.visualListsContainer.innerHTML = \"\";\n820: \n821:     const scopeFrames = step.scopeFrames || [];\n822:     const memoryModel = step.memoryModel || { heapObjects: [], gcObjects: [], totalUnreferencedCount: 0 };\n823: \n824:     // 1. Render Scope Isolation Cards (Show Local Scope on top of Global Scope, like a call stack)\n825:     const orderedScopes = [...scopeFrames].reverse();\n826:     if (orderedScopes.length === 0) {\n827:       this.scopeFramesContainer.innerHTML = `<div style=\"color:var(--text-muted); font-size:13px;\">No active scopes</div>`;\n828:     } else {\n829:       orderedScopes.forEach((sc) => {\n830:         const isLocal = sc.scopeType === \"LOCAL\";\n831:         const card = document.createElement(\"div\");\n832:         card.className = `scope-frame-card ${isLocal ? \"is-local-scope\" : \"is-global-scope\"} ${\n833:           sc.isActive ? \"is-active-scope\" : \"is-inactive-scope\"\n834:         }`;\n835: \n836:         const headerBadge = sc.isActive ? \"ACTIVE SCOPE\" : \"PARENT SCOPE\";\n837:         const vars = sc.variables || [];\n838: \n839:         let rowsHTML = \"\";\n840:         if (vars.length === 0) {\n841:           rowsHTML = `\n842:             <div class=\"scope-var-row\" style=\"grid-template-columns: 1fr; color:var(--text-muted); text-align:center;\">\n843:               No variables bound in this scope yet\n844:             </div>\n845:           `;\n846:         } else {\n847:           rowsHTML = vars\n848:             .map((v) => {\n849:               const isChanged = sc.isActive && (v.status === \"created\" || v.status === \"updated\");\n850:               const pill =\n851:                 isChanged && v.status === \"created\"\n852:                   ? `<span class=\"changed-pill\">New</span>`\n853:                   : isChanged && v.status === \"updated\"\n854:                   ? `<span class=\"changed-pill\">Changed</span>`\n855:                   : \"\";\n856:               const valPreview = Array.isArray(v.rawValue)\n857:                 ? `list[${v.rawValue.length}]`\n858:                 : `${v.type}: ${v.current}`;\n859:               return `\n860:                 <div class=\"scope-var-row ${isChanged ? \"var-row-changed\" : \"\"}\">\n861:                   <span class=\"var-name-cell\">${this.escapeHTML(v.name)}${pill}</span>\n862:                   <span class=\"ref-arrow-badge\" title=\"Variable '${this.escapeHTML(\n863:                     v.name\n864:                   )}' points to Heap Address ${this.escapeHTML(v.address || \"@0x1000\")}\">\n865:                     ──► ${this.escapeHTML(v.address || \"@0x1000\")}\n866:                   </span>\n867:                   <span class=\"var-val-preview\" title=\"${this.escapeHTML(v.current)}\">\n868:                     ${this.escapeHTML(valPreview)}\n869:                   </span>\n870:                 </div>\n871:               `;\n872:             })\n873:             .join(\"\");\n874:         }\n875: \n876:         card.innerHTML = `\n877:           <div class=\"scope-frame-header\">\n878:             <span>${this.escapeHTML(sc.title)}</span>\n879:             <span class=\"scope-active-tag\">${headerBadge}</span>\n880:           </div>\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":372,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T11:41:47Z","input_tokens":3527,"cache_read_tokens":137562,"output_tokens":3741,"thinking":"In the active scope card, variables marked \"created\" or \"updated\" within a step should not appear as changed within a substep where `varsBeforeStep` is true. Specifically, \"created\" variables should not show any changes initially, as they were not present before. Likewise, \"updated\" variables present before the step shouldn't register an immediate change at the substep level.\n\n\nAdded new elements to the DOM initialization to support teaching substeps and explanations. Initialized `currentSubstepIdx` in the constructor. Updated event bindings to control navigation between substeps when previous, next, step, or restart buttons are clicked.\n\n\nThe system needs to reset to the first step and substep upon manual restart, or when the trace completes automatically. Keyboard events are handled to navigate substeps using arrow keys and the F7 key. The `startAutoPlay` function is updated to use the `goToNextSubstep` function. The `goToNextSubstep` and `goToPrevSubstep` functions define the logic for stepping through substeps and steps within a trace, handling boundary conditions and rendering the appropriate step at each stage.\n\n\nThe navigation logic now manages stepping through substeps within each step of the trace, handling potential edge cases where the trace is empty.  The `goToStep` function limits the target step index within the trace bounds. `renderStep` handles the rendering of substeps.\n\n\nThe `renderStep` function updates the UI elements based on the current step and substep. It handles displaying the step progress, enabling/disabling navigation buttons based on the current position. Scope indicators are updated with the appropriate local/global scope labels based on step context. Also calls functions to render code, teaching materials, memory/scopes, and iterations within specific UI areas.\n\n\nThe teaching area's content is now generated based on the current step or substep lesson. The title, code snippet, and expression evaluator are rendered using appropriate lesson data, while handling potential null values. The calculation breakdown card visibility is controlled and its data populated, ensuring no display issues occur when a card isn't present. \"What is happening\" and \"Why is this operation necessary\" sections are formatted and rendered based on lesson content availability.\n\n\nThe teaching area content is constructed, displaying \"why necessary\" explanations, variable states, and next step descriptions derived from the lesson data. The final answer banner is displayed conditionally, using data from a lesson's `finalBanner` if present.\n\nMemory and scope visualizations are generated by clearing existing containers. Scope frames are rendered, reversing the order. No active scopes are indicated if no frames exist. The `varsBeforeStep` flag determines if changes from the previous substep should be shown.\n\n\nScope frame cards are constructed, differentiating local and global scopes and their active status, with appropriate headers. Variable rows are generated; variables created during the current step are hidden in \"before\" substeps, as these are new and shouldn't be presented as \"changed\" initially. Variable change indicators are implemented, showing \"New\" or \"Changed\" pills only when variables have been newly created or updated in the current step, unless `useBeforeVars` is set.\n\n\nVariable previews are generated for scope frames, indicating value types and array lengths. Heap addresses are also displayed for reference. The active number in a list highlights the corresponding index value during iteration, linked to the real list. Focus shifts to lines 80-145 in the relevant file.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\app.js","EndLine":145,"StartLine":80,"toolAction":"Viewing app.js initDOM elements","toolSummary":"View app.js lines 80-145"}}]}
